A||N||9||Will||GM 4 channel ABS on Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||Will||09-26-2000||11:02 PM||||What was the first car GM made with 4 channel ABS?<BR>     I want to see if I can adapt GM ABS hardware to my car; and of course provide the info to other members of the Fiero community.<BR>     I would like to have four channel ABS, though I need it to be as early as possible. Early ABS used controllers separate from the ECM. Late model ABS controllers are integrated into the PCM, at least that's what I have been led to believe.<BR>     Could I use a late model PCM without a late model engine? Would the ABS still work if I just supplied 12 volts and ABS sensor inputs without hooking it up to an engine?<BR>     Terryk, do you know anything about this topic?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||09-28-2000||12:54 AM||||Try a late 80's S-10 they have the 2 channel ABS if you got the rear ABS to work then move onto the 4 wheel ABS.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-28-2000||06:02 PM||||You have to watch out for truck ABS. Allot of times what they call ABS on trucks is really a proportioning valve with a linkage to the axle. As you load the truck it gives more rear brake. unload the truck and rear braking is reduced. It's to prevent the wheels locking when the truck is empty. It's not true ABS like allot of people are led to believe.<P>You can tell really quick if it's the valve job. look for a thin linkage from the rear axle connected to a block up on the body with a couple steel lines attached. It's easy to spot.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||09-28-2000||08:46 PM||||In the Jan. 1999 issue of Hot Rod magazine, page 84. a guy named Pete Mungo did all sorts of cool things to his 69 AMX. One of which had a '96 Vette ABS system. It uses a standalone computer for the ABS and traction control. He used Volvo reluctor rings and BMW sensors. You can also add the traction control, which is a real improvement if you don't hook up the timing retard and just use the throttle and brake controls. He also used the MC and booster from the Vette, but I'm not sure if it's neccesary.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||09-28-2000||10:53 PM||||Do any older trucks have real ABS? Is there such a thing as two channel ABS? A pair of such systems might work.<BR>     Do I get traction control whether I want it or not with the Vette setup? I'm not big on the idea of traction control, although I might be able to rig it to be switchable. How does it cut throttle? Are '96 vettes drive by wire?<BR>     Probably will not be able to use vette booster, though I have heard the MC will bolt up with tubing mods.<P>     Thanks for the responses||||reg||5
Z||000005||Formula 18||09-29-2000||04:53 AM||||Umm, I thought I read an article about the Newer vette's where did had a drivre do test laps around a cousre they set up in a lot "autocross style" to see how they could turn the fastest laps. With ABS & Traction on, one with just ABS and one in "driver's mode"  with nothing on. <P>So I think if you get the right box you can switch it on and off as you wish. <P>Let us know how it turns out. I am interusted in seeing it work. <P>Goodluck, <P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-29-2000||05:56 AM||||I've never seen a 2 channel at all. 3 4 or more never 2. (3 chan uses a pickup on the driveshaft of RWD cars.)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Pontiaddict||09-29-2000||10:40 AM||||The article says that the computer is for both ABS and traction control. It applies the brakes, tells the computer to back off the timing,(defeatable since you won't hook it up to the fiero computer) and through a cable cuts back on the throttle. It is swithcable, but I think that it defaults in the ON position every time you start the car.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Will||09-29-2000||12:00 PM||||Formula 18:<BR>     That was a 97+ Vette with LS1 and drive-by-wire.<P>Pontiaddict:<BR>     I don't have to hook up the throttle cable for it either, but I dont want it applying the brakes for traction control, just ABS.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Will||09-30-2000||06:24 PM||||How is the ABS handled in early FWD (e.g. Sunbird)? How does three channel ABS work on those cars since they don't have a driveshaft?<P>||||reg||1
